gpui_windows: park the vsync thread while no window wants frames

Base: zed-industries/zed a84689073d296dfd39987bc7dd478e43ef76d83a (2026-10-03).
Draft prepared in the FastPDF repository (docs/upstream-issues/gpui-idle.md);
not submitted anywhere. Apply from the root of a zed checkout with `git apply`.
This file carries no author: a commit made from it with `git commit` or
`git format-patch` gets the local git identity (user.name / user.email).

The VSyncProvider thread invalidated every window on every vblank, so an idle
window woke the UI thread at the refresh rate only for `request_frame` to find
nothing to draw. Implement `PlatformWindow::frame_waker` on Windows and let the
vsync thread park once no window has requested a frame for one second; a request
unparks it and windows are invalidated right away. While parked it wakes once a
second to detect a lost device. Direct Manipulation contacts, running gestures
and draws deferred by the DrawCoordinator also request frames.

